; Stag — AnimalDefinition data entry (gdd.md -> Data Schemas / Content Architecture).
; Roster row: roster.md -> Already-Defined Roster | Ruled: decisions.md -> D-43.
; Asset: Quaternius "Ultimate Animated Animal Pack", CC0 1.0 Universal — see
;   project/attribution/sources/quaternius_ultimate_animated_animals.tres.
;
; SPECIES CHOICE: red deer (Cervus elaphus) — "stag" is specifically the term for an adult
; male red deer, which is also the species docs/content/cleared-pool-fact-cards.md § Stag
; sources against (ADW + The Wildlife Trusts).
;
; CAPACITY FIELDS (D-43): capacity_radius = 0 -> SENTINEL `CAPACITY_RADIUS_FOLLOWS_SCOUT`,
; meaning "equal to scout_radius" (12), not a radius of zero. Three habitat tags
; (forest + cover + rocks) deliberately mirror Fox's "hardest habitat" framing one tag
; harder; max_individuals = 3 (half the roster's ~6 baseline) plus the pool's highest
; tiles_per_individual (8) makes art.md's "rare trophy" framing literal through scarcity.
; Not farm-tolerant.
;
; fact_text is docs/content/cleared-pool-fact-cards.md § Stag's proposed line, transcribed
; verbatim — all four checklist steps PASS there. Per-clause sourcing:
;   "male red deer"                          -> Wildlife Trusts, "A male red deer is
;                                                called a 'stag'..."
;   "grows a brand-new set ... every year"    -> ADW ("widely branching antlers ... found
;                                                on males only"); Wildlife Trusts ("Within
;                                                a few weeks of shedding old antlers, new
;                                                ones will start to grow.")
;   "bigger than the year before"             -> Wildlife Trusts ("increasing in size as
;                                                they get older")
; https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Cervus_elaphus/
; https://www.wildlifetrusts.org/wildlife-explorer/mammals/red-deer
; A combat-adjacent clause (rutting/fighting) on the same Wildlife Trusts page was cut
; entirely, not softened — see the source file's Checklist step 4.
;
; news_reports intentionally empty — News Report pools for this pool are a separate, later
; purchase (not part of Content Pipeline step 4/5 for this dispatch).
;
; TIERS — RE-SPEC 2026-09-04 (habitat tiers). THE DESIGN'S CENTREPIECE.
;
; PROPOSAL, NOT A DECISION. Every divisor, radius and cap below is this design's own
; first-pass proposal awaiting human sign-off, per the project rule that all tuning values
; are the human's. Source: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-habitat-tiers-design.md § 9,
; § 12 (OQ-A, ruled 2026-09-04).
;
; `deer/4` IS AN ORDINARY HABITAT NEED against a RESIDENT-emitted tag — no new machinery
; required at all, the same mechanic `people` already uses. Deer.tres emits `deer` (see
; that file); this need means a stag cannot appear until four deer already live here, and
; a fifth stag would need twenty. Rarity stops being a hand-tuned `max_individuals` alone
; and becomes something the player earns by building a real deer population first.
; `rocks` was DROPPED from the original three-tag proposal (forest + cover + rocks,
; mirroring Fox one tag harder): with the deer gate doing the distinguishing work, a fourth
; requirement made stags near-unreachable rather than rare (spec § 9).
;
; Single tier "rare": `open_grass/5` `forest/3` `deer/4`, gated by `!built<=0`, ALL AT
; RADIUS 14 (the spec table's own `@14` — a stag reads the wider neighbourhood a deer
; population lives across, not just its own tile). Adds one edge to the acyclicity check
; (deer -> deer -> stag); see `HabitatGraph.find_cycle()`.
;
; The legacy flat fields (habitat_needs / tiles_per_individual / max_individuals) are LEFT
; IN PLACE and are now inert: `effective_tiers()` prefers `tiers` when non-empty. They are
; retained so a rollback is a one-line edit rather than a re-authoring.
[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="AnimalDefinition" load_steps=10 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/definitions/animal_definition.gd" id="1_schema"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://assets/animals/stag/Stag.tscn" id="2_model"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/definitions/habitat_need.gd" id="3_need"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/definitions/habitat_limit.gd" id="4_limit"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/definitions/habitat_tier.gd" id="5_tier"]

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="need_rare_grass"]
script = ExtResource("3_need")
tag = "open_grass"
radius = 14
tiles_per_individual = 5

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="need_rare_forest"]
script = ExtResource("3_need")
tag = "forest"
radius = 14
tiles_per_individual = 3

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="need_rare_deer"]
script = ExtResource("3_need")
tag = "deer"
radius = 14
tiles_per_individual = 4

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="limit_rare_built"]
script = ExtResource("4_limit")
tag = "built"
radius = 14
max_count = 0

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="tier_rare"]
script = ExtResource("5_tier")
id = "rare"
needs = Array[Resource]([SubResource("need_rare_grass"), SubResource("need_rare_forest"), SubResource("need_rare_deer")])
limits = Array[Resource]([SubResource("limit_rare_built")])
max_individuals = 2
arrival_group_size = 1

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_schema")
id = "stag"
display_name = "Stag"
habitat_needs = Array[String](["forest", "cover", "rocks"])
personality = "Shy"
avoids = Array[String]([])
farm_tolerant = false
scout_radius = 12
capacity_radius = 0
tiles_per_individual = 8
max_individuals = 3
tiers = Array[Resource]([SubResource("tier_rare")])
emits_tags = Array[String]([])
model_scenes = Array[PackedScene]([ExtResource("2_model")])
fact_text_pool = Array[String](["A stag is a male red deer, and every year it grows a brand-new set of branching antlers that are bigger than the year before."])
news_reports = Array[String]([])
